//
// What the Markdown in this repository is held to.
//
// Two deliberate departures from the defaults, and nothing else:
//
//   line-length  off. Prose is written one sentence per line and never wrapped to a column, so a
//                diff shows the sentence that changed; a sentence too long to read is split into
//                two sentences, not wrapped.
//
//   no-inline-html  off, and with it first-line-h1. The README opens with a licence header and a
//                   centred image, which Markdown has no way of expressing and GitHub renders as
//                   HTML — so the first line is a comment rather than a heading, on purpose.
{
  "config": {
    "line-length": false,
    "no-inline-html": false,
    "first-line-heading": false
  },
  "globs": ["**/*.md", "!target"]
}
